From: Richard Murillo <6811113+rjmurillo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:47:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(rules): sync corpus byte figures and stale date range

Continuation of the adr-review panel fix round (5 of 6 seats Block).
Two more analyst-triaged stale-doc findings from the same review:

KOH: `.agents/governance/FAILURE-MODES.md`'s intro paragraph claimed the
catalog spanned "December 2025 through January 2026", but the Index
table's own evidence cites incidents through 2026-06 (pattern 11) and
issue #5404 dated 2026-08 (pattern 12, this PR). Updated the range to
"December 2025 through August 2026" to match the Index table's own
evidence-file dates.

Corpus byte-figure sync: the prior commit (eae055405) tightened
`builder-ethos.md`/`voice.md`, changing the always-on mirror total from
70,392 to 70,417 bytes and the `.claude/rules/` source total from
70,508 to 70,533 bytes. `.claude/rules/canonical-source-mirror.md` and
`.serena/memories/architecture/always-on-membership-lives-in-the-mirror.md`
both hand-state these figures in a two-row table; both were still on the
pre-fix numbers. Updated both to 70,417 / 70,417 / 70,533 (delta
unchanged at 116, per test_doctrine_source_basis_figure_and_delta_are_consistent).

Regenerated `.github/instructions/canonical-source-mirror.instructions.md`
and its `src/copilot-cli/instructions` mirror via build_all.py; git diff
confirms the mirrors match source with zero drift.

Verification: `instruction_budget.py --ci` exits 0 (656 bytes headroom);
`pytest tests/validation/test_always_on_corpus_claims.py` 37 passed,
confirming both trees and all hand-stated figures agree with a live
measurement.

--no-verify: same documented files.pythonhosted.org TLS handshake
failure blocking `uv run --frozen` as the immediately prior commit in
this branch (eae055405) and commit 3afa072c4. Ran instruction_budget.py
--ci and the corpus claims test suite manually instead; both pass.

